course: dictionary
lesson: 39
title: Acceptable: good enough or allowed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Acceptable means good enough or allowed. Something acceptable is something most people agree is fine, or something that is within the rules.
explain: At school, behaviour can be acceptable or not acceptable. «Hitting is not acceptable» because it hurts people, so it is not allowed and not fine.
explain: «A dare does not make a rude act acceptable; the person who does it is still responsible.» A dare does not make the rude act fine or allowed, so the blame stays with the person who did it. To check your meaning, swap in "fine or allowed": "does not make a rude act fine" still makes sense.
fact: «Acceptable» means good enough or allowed.
fact: «Acceptable» can describe behaviour that most people agree is fine and polite.
fact: «Not acceptable» means not allowed and not fine.
fact: In maths and science, an acceptable answer or error is one that is within the allowed range.
fact: Useful phrases: «perfectly acceptable», «socially acceptable», «acceptable to».
exercise: «Hitting is not acceptable at school.» What does not acceptable mean here? | Easy to forget | Very quiet and calm | Very good at sport | *Not allowed and not fine
exercise: «A dare does not make a rude act acceptable.» What does acceptable mean here? | Brave and bold | *Fine or allowed | Loud and noisy | Free to buy
exercise: Sam says his answer is within the allowed range in maths, so it is acceptable. What does acceptable mean for an answer? | A question with no answer | Written in neat handwriting | The biggest number | *Within the allowed range
test: Which phrase describes behaviour that most people agree is fine and polite? | Very, very small | Hard to reach | *Socially acceptable | Unexpectedly loud
test: «A dare does not make a rude act acceptable; the person who does it is still responsible.» Who is responsible? | *The person who does the rude act | Nobody at all | The teacher | The dare-giver only
exam: Tom's sketch is not perfect, but it is an acceptable sketch for homework. What does acceptable mean here? | Ready for the bin | Very expensive | Painted in blue | *Good enough
